  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B049",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B012",
    "B003"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. Optical lattice clocks are a complete experimental advance: magic-wavelength confinement enables long interrogation while controlling motional shifts, and independent laboratories have reproducibly reached the 10^-18 regime. This is a new measurement capability already used for precision tests and relativistic geodesy, not a promise dependent on a future standards decision. Katori's defining lattice-clock concept and Ye's decisive high-performance experimental development give an unusually compact and coherent attribution. The historical review requested by the chair should test this boundary carefully, but the evidence presented still supports these two distinct central contributions.",
    "case_against": "The citation must remain limited to optical lattice clocks and not absorb the broader, multi-contributor development of optical-frequency metrology. We should also establish whether an early experimental contributor is indispensable to the original realization; if so, the proposed two-person allocation would need reconsideration. A redefinition of the second and particular downstream applications should not be treated as necessary grounds for the award.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce prefers WMAP because its precision mapping gave the standard cosmological model durable empirical footing, while recognizing the difficulty of representing a collaboration-scale measurement with three names.",
        "response": "WMAP is a formidable mature measurement achievement, but its attribution question is material: the proposed names must represent a large mission, measurement, and analysis enterprise. B049 has comparably strong reproducibility as an instrument-led advance while retaining a more sharply bounded physical innovation and a more readily testable two-person division of credit."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth favors the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase for making global quantum phase experimentally physical, while noting their distinct historical origins.",
        "response": "I agree fully on the depth and long experimental maturity of those effects. Her reservation remains important, however: joining two historically distinct discoveries requires a broad common framing. The lattice-clock case has a single experimental chain, from magic-wavelength quantum control to independently verified clocks, and therefore provides the cleaner public configuration."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that the reproducible lattice-clock platform and the Katori-Ye concept-to-development allocation are stronger at present than quantum error correction, whose scalable endpoint remains incomplete.",
        "response": "I concur. The relevant standard is not merely impressive precision but repeated realization of the same physical architecture as a functioning measurement instrument. That is already satisfied for B049; the citation should consequently recognize the lattice-clock invention and development, without claiming credit for all optical metrology."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical documentation confirms that Katori and Ye alone capture the decisive original concept and early realization, rather than requiring an additional early lattice-clock contributor.",
      "Where the citation should draw the boundary between optical lattice clocks and the earlier, broader development of optical-frequency metrology."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No recusal-requiring connection to the proposed B049 laureates is apparent from the supplied profile. My background in quantum optics and quantum information makes careful attention to experimental maturity appropriate, but does not create a disclosed personal or institutional conflict for this configuration."
  }
}
